<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p>
    <strong>App:</strong> Quick QR Scanner &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
    <strong>Developer:</strong> LLCAI Labs &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
    <strong>Contact:</strong>
    <a href="mailto:llcailabs@gmail.com">llcailabs@gmail.com</a>
    &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
    <strong>Last updated:</strong> 2026-08-27
</p>

<p>
    Quick QR Scanner is a utility application that decodes QR codes and
    one-dimensional barcodes (EAN-13, EAN-8, UPC-A, UPC-E, Code 128,
    Code 39, Code 93, ITF, PDF417, Aztec, Data Matrix) using the
    device camera or an image picked from the gallery.
</p>

<p>
    The application is provided by LLCAI Labs, a sole proprietor based in
    Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia.
</p>

<p>
    This policy describes the data that Quick QR Scanner collects, stores,
    transmits, and shares with third parties. It is written in plain English
    so anyone can read it without legal training.
</p>


<h2>1. The short version</h2>

<blockquote>
    By default, Quick QR Scanner stores nothing on any network server.
    The scans you perform, the gallery images you decode, and the app
    settings you choose all live locally on your device.
    Ads are served by Google AdMob at the bottom of the Home and History
    screens.
</blockquote>

<p>
    The App does not require an account and does not collect personal data
    on its own servers beyond what may be processed by third-party services
    used to provide advertising.
</p>


<h2>2. Data we collect</h2>

<h3>2.1 Data stored locally on your device</h3>

<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Scan results</strong> — the raw value decoded from the QR
        or barcode, the detected format, and the wall-clock time of the scan
        are stored in a local SQLite (Room) database inside the application's
        sandbox.
    </li>

    <li>
        <strong>Settings</strong> — vibration toggle, scan sound toggle,
        auto-open URLs toggle, and theme preference (System / Light / Dark)
        are persisted via Jetpack DataStore Preferences in the application's
        sandbox.
    </li>

    <li>
        The <strong>Privacy Policy</strong> row in the About section of
        Settings opens this privacy policy URL. This does not store additional
        data.
    </li>
</ul>

<p>
    None of the items above are uploaded to LLCAI Labs servers.
    Removing the application also removes the locally stored data.
</p>


<h3>2.2 Data processed by the camera pipeline</h3>

<p>
    Quick QR Scanner uses the device camera with the
    <code>android.permission.CAMERA</code> permission granted by you at
    runtime. Google's bundled ML Kit Barcode Scanning library is used to
    detect and decode QR codes and barcodes.
</p>

<p>
    Camera frames are processed entirely on-device and are not uploaded to
    LLCAI Labs servers.
</p>

<p>
    The bundled ML Kit models are included inside the application and run
    locally on the device.
</p>


<h3>2.3 Data processed when an advertisement is shown</h3>

<p>
    Banner advertisements are served by
    <strong>Google Mobile Ads (AdMob)</strong> on the Home and History screens.
</p>

<p>
    Depending on the user's device settings, applicable laws, consent choices,
    and Google's advertising systems, AdMob may process information such as:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Advertising ID (GAID), where available.</li>
    <li>IP address or IP-derived approximate location.</li>
    <li>Ad impression information.</li>
    <li>Ad interaction and click information.</li>
    <li>Information required for advertising, fraud prevention, measurement,
        and attribution.</li>
</ul>

<p>
    These data are processed by Google according to Google's applicable
    privacy policies and advertising technologies. LLCAI Labs does not
    directly receive the raw AdMob event stream; we may receive aggregated
    reporting information through the AdMob publisher dashboard.
</p>


<h3>2.4 Data the App does not collect</h3>

<ul>
    <li>Name, email address, phone number, or postal address as part of normal app operation.</li>
    <li>Account creation information.</li>
    <li>Payment information.</li>
    <li>Microphone data.</li>
    <li>Contacts.</li>
    <li>Precise GPS location.</li>
    <li>Photo or video content beyond an image explicitly selected by the user for scanning.</li>
</ul>


<h2>3. Third parties we work with</h2>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Third party</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Information that may be processed</th>
            <th>Trigger</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>Google AdMob</td>
            <td>Advertising, measurement and attribution</td>
            <td>
                Advertising identifiers, IP-derived approximate location,
                ad impressions, interactions and related advertising metadata
            </td>
            <td>
                When an advertisement is requested or displayed
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p>
    Quick QR Scanner does not embed separate analytics, social-login,
    crash-reporting, or attribution SDKs operated by LLCAI Labs.
</p>

<p>
    ML Kit Barcode Scanning is bundled with the application and performs
    barcode scanning on-device during normal operation.
</p>


<h2>4. Children</h2>

<p>
    Quick QR Scanner is not specifically designed for or marketed to children
    under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information
    from children through our own servers.
</p>

<p>
    If you believe that information relating to a child has been provided
    to LLCAI Labs, please contact us at
    <a href="mailto:llcailabs@gmail.com">llcailabs@gmail.com</a>.
</p>


<h2>5. Your rights and controls</h2>

<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>View scan history</strong> — the History screen displays
        saved scans stored on your device.
    </li>

    <li>
        <strong>Delete a single scan</strong> — delete an individual
        scan from the History screen.
    </li>

    <li>
        <strong>Delete all scans</strong> — use the
        <em>Clear all scan history</em> option in Settings.
    </li>

    <li>
        <strong>Control advertising preferences</strong> — Android and
        Google provide device-level controls for advertising personalization.
    </li>

    <li>
        <strong>Reset your advertising ID</strong> — Android provides
        advertising-ID controls through the device's privacy settings.
    </li>

    <li>
        <strong>Uninstall</strong> — uninstalling the application removes
        locally stored scan history and settings from the device.
    </li>

    <li>
        <strong>Contact us</strong> — for privacy questions or requests,
        email
        <a href="mailto:llcailabs@gmail.com">llcailabs@gmail.com</a>.
    </li>
</ul>


<h2>6. Data retention</h2>

<ul>
    <li>
        Scan history remains on the device until deleted by the user or
        until the application is uninstalled.
    </li>

    <li>
        Settings remain on the device until the application is uninstalled
        or application data is cleared.
    </li>

    <li>
        Information processed by Google AdMob is retained according to
        Google's applicable policies and retention practices.
    </li>
</ul>


<h2>7. Data transit and security</h2>

<p>
    Network traffic used by the application and its advertising SDKs is
    transmitted using encrypted network connections where supported by
    the relevant service.
</p>

<p>
    Scan history and application settings are stored inside the application's
    private Android storage area. Quick QR Scanner does not upload scan
    history to LLCAI Labs servers.
</p>


<h2>8. International transfers</h2>

<p>
    LLCAI Labs is based in Malaysia. Third-party services such as Google
    AdMob may process information on servers located outside Malaysia or
    the user's home jurisdiction.
</p>

<p>
    Such processing is governed by the applicable policies and terms of
    those third-party providers.
</p>


<h2>9. Camera permission</h2>

<p>
    Quick QR Scanner requests the
    <code>android.permission.CAMERA</code> permission when the scanner
    requires camera access.
</p>

<p>
    If you deny the permission, the scanner displays a camera-permission
    message and does not capture camera frames.
</p>

<p>
    The <strong>Scan from gallery</strong> function uses the Android system
    Photo Picker and does not require camera access.
</p>


<h2>10. Policy updates</h2>

<p>
    If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top of this page
    and provide a short description of material changes where appropriate.
</p>


